# Packages blocked from auto-upgrade (require manual migration).
#
# NOTE: do NOT add entries for versions that are merely too fresh. check-deps.ts
# reads the .ci/config/release-age.json window and automatically defers (does not fail on)
# any `latest` published inside that window — npm cannot install it yet anyway,
# and it clears itself once the version ages out. Only blocklist packages held
# back for a real reason (breaking major, native rebuild, pin conflict, etc.).
#
# Format: package-name  # BLOCKER: <substantive reason>
#
# The BLOCKER convention is enforced by scripts/lib/blocker-validator.ts
# (invoked from scripts/gates/check-deps.ts): each line needs a 30+ char reason
# that does not match the banned-phrase list. Blank line = end of group.
#
# To upgrade a blocked package: remove its line from this file and run
#   npm run check:deps -- --upgrade

# ESLint v10 — blocked until typescript-eslint, eslint-plugin-import, eslint-plugin-react support v10
@eslint/js  # BLOCKER: v10.x requires eslint v10; typescript-eslint/import/react plugins lack v10 peer dep support

# Astro/React integration
@astrojs/react  # BLOCKER: 6.x is a major on the Astro integration stack while astro itself is deliberately held on the 5 line (see the astro entry below); move it with that migration, not standalone. Only the major is blocked — in-range 5.0.x patches still upgrade normally.
@astrojs/mdx  # BLOCKER: v5.x requires astro@^6.0.0; we are on astro 5.x and astro v6 migration is not scheduled
astro  # BLOCKER: www is built on the astro 5 line; v6/v7 are breaking majors covering the whole site build — same unscheduled-migration hold as @astrojs/mdx, take them together as a dedicated project

# glob is pinned by the root overrides entry (see package.json _overridesReasons.glob)
glob  # BLOCKER: root overrides force glob ^11 tree-wide and npm EOVERRIDE requires the declared devDep range to equal the override, so the v13 major cannot be taken until the override family is re-evaluated

# @types/node major must match Node engine version (22.x)
@types/node  # BLOCKER: v25+ targets Node 25 APIs; our engines field and CI runners are on Node 22

# eslint-plugin-unicorn v66 — major release with new/renamed lint rules
eslint-plugin-unicorn  # BLOCKER: v66 is a major release that adds and renames lint rules which would surface new violations across the whole monorepo; adoption deferred to a dedicated lint-tooling PR that audits and fixes the rule-set changes

# playwright — E2E/test runner; any version bump changes the bundled browser revisions
playwright  # BLOCKER: a playwright version bump changes the bundled browser revisions, so it is never a drop-in dependency bump — the pinned browsers must be re-downloaded (npx playwright install) and the E2E/bridge suites re-validated against the new revisions in the same change; take any future bump together with that test-infra revalidation
@playwright/test  # BLOCKER: same hold as playwright above, and not a separate judgement call — @playwright/test@X depends on playwright@X pinned EXACTLY (verified: @playwright/test@1.62.0 -> "playwright": "1.62.0"), so upgrading it upgrades the browser revisions the entry above defers. Listing only `playwright` left the gate demanding the bump through its sibling; move both with the E2E/bridge revalidation.
# ESLint v10 core — same constraint as @eslint/js: plugin ecosystem lacks v10 support
eslint  # BLOCKER: v10 requires typescript-eslint/import/react plugin majors that have no eslint v10 peer support yet; take together with @eslint/js in a dedicated lint-tooling PR


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# private/account, SCOPED ENTRIES (`<dir>:<package>`).
#
# These are console-side policy about ANOTHER repository's dependencies, which
# reads oddly and is honest: it records a real external constraint rather than
# inventing one. private/account is under an operator freeze, so nothing here can
# be upgraded from this wave, and `check:deps --upgrade` has no scope flag and
# would write straight into that submodule.
#
# SCOPED, NOT BARE, and this is the load-bearing part: four of the seven
# (@biomejs/biome, typescript, vitest, hono) are ALSO console's own dependencies.
# A bare entry is keyed on the package name alone and would have silently stopped
# this gate reporting them for the CONSOLE tree ever again -- weakening a live
# check to record a constraint in a different repo. A `private/account:` prefix is
# consulted only when categorising that directory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
private/account:vitest  # BLOCKER: private/account is under an operator freeze (see rediacc/account#87); this is also a MAJOR, 4.1.11 -> 5.0.0, so it needs its own upgrade pass with the test suite driven, not a dependency refresh riding a CI-port wave. Waits for the freeze to lift; not a decision this wave is making.
private/account:typescript  # BLOCKER: private/account is under an operator freeze (see rediacc/account#87); this is also a MAJOR, 6.0.3 -> 7.0.2, which moves the compiler under the account worker and needs its own pass. Waits for the freeze to lift; not a decision this wave is making.
private/account:@biomejs/biome  # BLOCKER: private/account is under an operator freeze (see rediacc/account#87). Routine 2.5.11 -> 2.5.13 and it would be a one-line bump, but the freeze is an operator ruling about that repository and a lead cannot grant an exception to it while the operator is away. Console's own biome is NOT blocked -- that is why this entry is scoped.
private/account:hono  # BLOCKER: private/account is under an operator freeze (see rediacc/account#87). Routine 4.13.5 -> 4.13.7. Scoped so console's own hono keeps being checked.
private/account:stripe  # BLOCKER: private/account is under an operator freeze (see rediacc/account#87). Routine 22.6.1 -> 22.6.2, payment SDK, account-only.
private/account:@aws-sdk/client-s3  # BLOCKER: private/account is under an operator freeze (see rediacc/account#87). Routine 3.1124.0 -> 3.1131.0, account-only, and it moves in lockstep with the presigner below.
private/account:@aws-sdk/s3-request-presigner  # BLOCKER: private/account is under an operator freeze (see rediacc/account#87). Routine 3.1121.0 -> 3.1131.0, account-only, and the AWS SDK requires this to match client-s3 exactly.
private/account:nodemailer  # BLOCKER: v10 is a major on private/account's outbound mail path, where the SES transport and the rendered-template call sites are exercised only by the live email flows rather than by unit tests, so the bump needs a real send-path verification rather than a version bump; @types/nodemailer is on the 8.x line and tracks v9's shape, so both move together or neither does.
